<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">An-Nasir Yusuf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1228–1260</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as al-Nasir Yusuf</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An-Nasir Yusuf was the last major Ayyubid ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> from 1236 and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> from 1250. He reunited much of Ayyubid Syria but failed to recover <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a>. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a> invaded in 1260 he fled, was captured and was executed later that year.</p></div>
